{
  "scope": "One predeclared apparent-geocentric SPA substitution on 59 previously exposed annuals. Reference implementation and scoring checks pass; the calendar replacement gate fails. No new official-calendar requests or notification/default promotion.",
  "planText": "# SPA astronomical-reference experiment\n\nDeclared before SPA calendar forecasts or scoring on 2026-09-26. Existing calendar observations are exposed development data, not a holdout.\n\n## One candidate and unchanged control\n\n`baseline` retains the current USNO daily UTC00 recipe exactly. `spa-utc00` substitutes the Reda/Andreas SPA apparent geocentric declination and equation of time at the identical daily solar-carrier UTC00 sample. The declared conversion is UT1=UTC and TT=UT1+69.184 seconds, constant for this experiment. This is a numerical convention, not a reconstructed Diyanet time-scale specification or a claim about future leap seconds. The official SPA worked example is verified separately with its specified deltaT=67 seconds.\n\nKeep daily spherical geometry, latitude/longitude, height model (none), horizon threshold, all angle and shadow rules, Temkin, five-hour limits, solstice envelopes, missing-window/last-real-night quotients, interpolation, carrier selection, IANA zones and nearest-minute rounding unchanged. All downstream numerical quantities and seasonal boundaries are recomputed from the candidate astronomy. Neither city offsets nor new curve parameters are fitted. Do not apply topocentric/refraction additions from a SPA zenith routine to the existing geocentric horizon recipe. Existing USNO continuous-Asr metadata stays diagnostic-only and is omitted from exported candidate timing evidence; it never chooses the prayer clock. The southern continuous solver is outside this daily-recipe experiment.\n\nThis is a compatibility experiment with a documented astronomical reference. Better physical solar coordinates need not reproduce the institutional calendar better. It is not a full continuous-event SPA prayer-time solver.\n\n## Inputs\n\nReuse the complete prior global-numerics50 corpus and append already-exposed Hobart, Apia, Nuku'alofa, Jakarta, Cape Town, Auckland, Iqaluit, Kathmandu, La Paz and Suva 2027 annuals. Deduplicate on original case identity and retain prior full-year coordinates. Anchorage2027 is already in prior50. No new calendar/API retrieval or institute contact. The prepared catalog and all reference mappings/provenance must be frozen before scoring. If an intended addition fails unchanged-baseline reconciliation, disclose and resolve the mapping; never quietly exclude a case based on SPA results.\n\nAll six calendar events and all original days/fields remain in the denominator. Keep printed-date and explicitly conditional evening-cycle source interpretations independently of predictions. They describe the same observations, not two datasets. Source00:00, unavailable fields and date ambiguity stay visible. Baseline raw/rounded output must reconcile with the public unchanged entry points and prior archives.\n\n## Outputs and attribution\n\nSave full candidate and control forecasts, raw UTC instants, rounded UTCs, availability, carrier date, raw declination/EOT/horizon events, adjusted horizon/night duration, seasonal branch, annual anchor metadata and rounding shifts. Separate intermediate model differences from calendar-minute error; the archive does not contain the institution's unrounded seconds. Hash code, constants, sources, references and forecasts before scoring.\n\nReport exact/within-one-minute counts, maximum, signed errors, newly missing values and paired gains/losses by case, event, region, cohort and total. Characterize where the astronomy perturbation is amplified by seasonal branches; no causal attribution of official residuals from mere correlation. Retain changes of branch, anchor, carrier, local event date and chronology as distinct diagnostics.\n\n## Verification and acceptance\n\nVerify official SPA intermediates with their printed precision and compare against a separately executed openly licensed implementation on a deterministic multi-year/time grid. Audit source-table licensing and attribution. Independently verify all scoring decisions, baseline reconciliation and representative raw calendar geometry; verify northern wiring and traces separately. Reusable source-free code/tests may be published even if the calendar candidate fails.\n\nRetain the existing conservative replacement gate: increase total exactness, with no loss of exact or within-one counts, no larger maximum and no new nonzero-source missingness at any case, case/event, event, region or cohort under either source-date interpretation. Preserve individual regressions even if an aggregate passes. A pass would justify further validation, not automatic institutional equivalence or notification eligibility. No new sources or automatic runtime/default promotion in this bounded experiment. If the candidate fails, publish full negative findings and preserve the baseline; do not tune another variant after seeing scores.\n",
